#### 1.Build your own "engine" that runs an AI chatbot
* When you use ChatGPter or any AI chatbot, there's a program running behind the scenes that takes your question, feeds it to the AI model, and sends back the answer — efficiently, even when thousands of people are asking questions at once. Normally you'd just use someone else's engine (like OpenAI's). This project is: build your own version of that engine for a small, free AI model. You'd figure out how to handle multiple people asking questions at the same time without slowing everything down, and how to stream the answer back word-by-word (like you see in ChatGPT). It's a deep dive into "how does the software around an AI model actually work," not the AI model itself.